se seven words  four or five are funny he cares that  much and your word choice is that  important a lot of your humor is going  to come in the economy of the expression  now when it comes to the economy of the  expression the next tip  is to understand your premise  what is the premise of your joke what is  the message of your joke what are you  trying to say  in this joke every joke should have a  premise it should have a baseline  of what is this joke about sum up this  joke in a single sentence or phrase  chris rock has said  that if people don't get your joke  it may be because they don't get your  premise so a way to really start to hone  and refine  all these wordy jokes that we have a  habit of creating is to ask yourself  okay what am i trying to say here what  is the premise  now what is the most efficient and funny  way  i can express that premise oh that was a  good tip  if you found that tip helpful go ahead  and hit that subscribe button  so more comments can find these tips all  right and the final tip  here my friends is to actually  transcribe your set and we talked about  this in  the last type 5 uh episode which if you  haven't heard it yet  go back check it out and you will learn  about how to actually structure  your five-minute set but when it comes  to transcribing your set  another helpful hint here is to actually  transcribe it  and then bold where all your punch lines  are  so now you can start to physically see  where all your punch lines are  so you can start to either get them  closer together or  if there's a big gap between them how  can you find new punch lines in between  these two punch lines  and it may come down to your word choice  it may come down to word economy where  you really start to ask yourself  are these words necessary and a bonus  tip  we have here is to actually  use your instincts is to actually  use your common conversational style  to refine your jokes so after you write  your joke  actually say the joke out loud 